  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\n\nRelief o  Friday will be short-lived. The surface front is \nprojected to waver back northward as a warm front Friday night \ninto Saturday, re-introducing triple-digit heat indices and \nscattered elevated warm-advection convection to start the \nweekend. \n\nA stronger, more potent shortwave trough is forecast to dig out\nof the Northern Plains Sunday into Monday, driving a sharper \nsurface cold front through the Mississippi Valley. While showers\nand thunderstorms may accompany the frontal passage, \ndeterministic models and global ensembles show remarkably strong\nconsensus for a deeper continental polar (cP) airmass to push \ninto the central U.S. early next week. This will usher in a \nperiod of below-normal temperatures, lower dewpoints, and an \nextended break from the active convective pattern by Monday and \nTuesday.",
